{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://paharlaya.github.io/riacorpinternational/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "FAQ", "item": "https://paharlaya.github.io/riacorpinternational/faq.html"}]}
</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is your minimum order quantity?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Our standard MOQ is one 20 ft container. That works out at roughly 18\u201322 MT for botanicals, 12\u201316 MT for compressed psyllium husk, and considerably less by weight for standardised extracts and peptides, where 500 kg is a workable first order."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I combine products in one container?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Within a pillar, yes \u2014 botanicals consolidate freely with each other, as do fibres and extracts. Across pillars it is usually cheaper not to, because the two portfolios clear through different gateways."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I place an order?\n          \n            Enquiry \u2014 product, grade, quantity, destination port, Incoterm\n            Quotation \u2014 proforma invoice within 24\u201348 hours\n            Sample \u2014 optional, and we recommend it for a first order\n            Confirm and pay \u2014 against the proforma, by LC or TT\n            Production and despatch \u2014 with container tracking shared\n          \n        \n        Do you publish a price list?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Agricultural prices move with crop, season and currency, so a published list would be wrong within a fortnight. We issue a personalised proforma invoice within 24\u201348 hours of your enquiry, valid for a stated period."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do you work with first-time buyers?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, and we would rather start small. Samples, a trial LCL consignment and flexible terms on a first order are all normal here. Every long-standing buyer was a first-time buyer once."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Are samples available before a bulk order?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, across every grade in both pillars. We strongly encourage it. Approving a sample is what makes the rest of the relationship straightforward."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What do samples cost?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The sample itself is free. You cover the international courier charge, typically USD 30\u201380 by DHL or FedEx depending on destination. If you have your own courier account we will ship on that instead."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long does a sample take to arrive?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Despatched within 2\u20133 working days. Transit is roughly 3\u20135 days to the Middle East, 4\u20137 days to Europe, 5\u20138 days to Africa and 5\u201310 days elsewhere."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Will the bulk order match the sample?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, and this is the commitment the whole business rests on. The sample is drawn from the same grade and specification that will be supplied in bulk, and a Certificate of Analysis accompanies every shipment so you can check it against what you approved."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What payment methods do you accept?\n          \n            LC \u2014 Letter of Credit, at sight or usance\n            TT \u2014 telegraphic transfer, typically 30% advance and 70% against a copy of the bill of lading\n            DP \u2014 Documents against Payment\n            DA \u2014 Documents against Acceptance, for established buyers\n          \n        \n        Which currency do you invoice in?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "USD by default, as the standard currency for agricultural commodity trade. EUR and AED can be arranged where it suits your banking."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I open a Letter of Credit?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, from any internationally recognised bank. We ask that the LC is irrevocable, allows partial shipment and transhipment, and carries a tolerance of plus or minus 5% on quantity and value \u2014 agricultural goods rarely load to the exact kilo."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is there volume pricing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, above roughly 100 MT per product, and for buyers placing regular monthly or quarterly orders. Repeat business earns better terms than a single large order."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long from order confirmation to shipment?\n          \n            Himalayan botanicals \u2014 12\u201318 working days\n            Psyllium husk and powder \u2014 15\u201320 working days\n            Berberine extract and collagen peptides \u2014 18\u201325 working days\n            Organic grades \u2014 add 5\u20137 days for transaction certification\n            Custom printed packaging \u2014 add 7\u201310 days\n          \n        \n        Which ports do you ship from?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Two corridors. Himalayan botanicals move through the Siliguri/Darjeeling transit hub and dispatch from Syama Prasad Mookerjee Port, Kolkata. Bio-nutrients, extracts and peptides clear directly through Mundra, Nhava Sheva (JNPT) or Chennai, whichever gives your cargo the best rotation."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long is ocean transit?\n          \n            Gulf states \u2014 7\u201312 days\n            Southeast Asia \u2014 10\u201316 days\n            East Africa \u2014 14\u201320 days\n            Europe and West Africa \u2014 20\u201328 days\n            North America \u2014 22\u201330 days\n            Australia and New Zealand \u2014 18\u201325 days\n          \n        \n        Which Incoterms do you offer?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "EXW, FOB, CFR/CNF and CIF. FOB and CIF cover most of what we do. Tell us which your freight forwarder prefers and we will quote on it."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do you provide shipment tracking?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Once the vessel sails you get the bill of lading with vessel and voyage number, the container number for live tracking, and the ETA at your discharge port."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What documents come with every shipment?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificate of origin, phytosanitary certificate, health certificate, certificate of analysis and quality inspection report. Fumigation and insurance certificates are added where the market or Incoterm requires them."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do you provide a phytosanitary certificate?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, issued by the Plant Quarantine Authority of India and included with every agricultural shipment at no extra charge."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How is the certificate of origin issued?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "By an authorised body \u2014 usually FIEO, a chamber of commerce, or the relevant Export Promotion Council. Where your country has a preferential trade agreement with India, we issue the preferential form so you can claim the duty benefit."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can you meet my country's specific customs requirements?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Requirements differ \u2014 legalisation at the consulate for some Gulf states, a certificate of inspection for EU organic, prior notice filing for the US. Tell us the destination and we will prepare accordingly rather than send a generic set."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What certifications do you hold?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "IEC, APEDA, FSSAI, GST, Spices Board RCMC and Star Export House status on the registration side, and BRC, ISO 22000:2018, HACCP, GMP and USFDA registration with FSMA/FSVP on the food-safety side. Organic, Kosher and Halal are issued per consignment."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do your products meet EU pesticide MRLs?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. EU maximum residue limits are the tightest we work to, so lots destined for Europe are tested for residues at an NABL-accredited laboratory before packing, and we will not ship a lot that fails."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Are your products Halal?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Botanicals and psyllium are plant-based with no animal content, so they are inherently Halal. Collagen peptides are not \u2014 marine and bovine grades each carry their own certification, which we issue with the consignment on request."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I arrange my own third-party inspection?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, and we encourage it. We work routinely with SGS, Intertek, Bureau Veritas, COTECNA and T\u00dcV S\u00dcD, and the container is held until the report clears."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do you keep quality consistent between shipments?\n          \n            Asset-integrated sourcing from the same verified growers and processing units\n            Grading against a written specification, not a verbal one\n            Cleaning, sorting and metal detection\n            Lot-wise testing at an NABL-accredited laboratory\n            Retention samples held against every lot\n            Certificate of analysis issued per lot, not per shipment\n          \n        \n        What packaging options are available?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Botanicals ship in 25 kg and 50 kg bags. Psyllium ships compressed in 15 kg, 25 kg and 50 lb HDPE laminated paper bags with a food-grade liner, or fibre drums for pharmaceutical grades. Extracts and peptides ship in 20\u201325 kg bags or drums."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the shelf life?\n          \n            Whole botanicals \u2014 24 months in original packing\n            Ground botanicals \u2014 18\u201324 months\n            Psyllium husk and powder \u2014 24 months\n            Berberine extract and collagen peptides \u2014 24 months\n          \n          All figures assume cool, dry storage away from direct sunlight and strong odours.\n        \n        What if a shipment arrives damaged or off-specification?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Notify us within 7 days of discharge with photographs and, where relevant, an independent lab report. We check it against the retention sample and the certificate of analysis for that lot."}}]}
</script>
